    (23, 2, 'Priya wrote a list of tools before the repair, so nobody had to search during the work.'),
    (24, 2, 'A sign at the station showed the new platform number; travelers paused to read it twice.'),
    (25, 2, 'The school garden grew mint, beans, and flowers. Each bed had a label beside its path.'),
    (26, 2, 'Dev tested the kite in a light breeze, but its tail needed one more careful knot.'),
    (27, 2, 'The ferry arrived late because the river was high. Its captain explained the delay calmly.'),
    (28, 2, 'Mira found two similar keys in a drawer; only one could open the old storage room.'),
    (29, 2, 'At the workshop, students measured each board before they cut it to fit the frame.'),
    (30, 2, 'A note on the door said the hall was closed today, but the side room remained open.'),
    (31, 2, 'The book cart visited on Friday. New readers learned its stops from a simple printed map.'),
    (32, 2, 'Nia checked the soil in both pots; the one near the wall needed less water.'),
    (33, 2, 'The clock ran slowly after lunch, so its owner recorded the time and watched it again.'),
    (34, 2, 'A group painted the park bench blue and waited until the next morning to use it.'),
    (35, 2, 'The first recipe was too sweet. Tara used less sugar when she baked the second batch.'),
    (36, 2, 'A runner stopped at the fountain, filled her bottle, and thanked the volunteer nearby.'),
    (37, 2, 'The town notice listed three meeting times. Farah circled the one she could attend.'),
    (38, 2, 'Clouds hid the stars at first, yet the sky cleared before the telescope was packed away.'),
    (39, 2, 'Two teams compared their paper bridges and wrote down which folds held the most coins.'),
    (40, 2, 'The visitor desk kept a spare umbrella for anyone caught by a sudden shower.'),
    (41, 3, 'The archive labeled each photograph with a date, a place, and the name of its donor.'),
    (42, 3, 'A minor change in the river''s course made the old survey map harder to interpret.'),
    (43, 3, 'The committee tested two routes, compared their travel times, and chose the safer crossing.'),
    (44, 3, 'When the first reading seemed unusual, Amita repeated the measurement before recording it.'),
    (45, 3, 'The lantern maker kept a sketch of every design, including those that failed to balance.'),
    (46, 3, 'At the rehearsal, one misplaced cue changed the scene; the stage crew corrected its timing.'),
    (47, 3, 'A volunteer counted the borrowed tools and noticed that the drill had not yet returned.'),
    (48, 3, 'The weather club moved its wind vane beyond the wall to obtain a clearer reading.'),
    (49, 3, 'Ezra revised the schedule after two families missed the cart''s final Friday stop.'),
    (50, 3, 'A careful label can distinguish an observed fact from a reasonable but uncertain guess.'),
    (51, 3, 'The glasshouse team recorded temperature at dawn, noon, and dusk for an entire week.'),
    (52, 3, 'Noor kept both dates on the letter; the writer had continued after midnight.'),
    (53, 3, 'A second estimate included anchors and repairs that the first estimate had omitted.'),
    (54, 3, 'The survey followed the path people actually used, not the straight line on an old plan.'),
    (55, 3, 'Because the workshop was noisy, the team practiced clear signals before starting work.'),
    (56, 3, 'The guide marked each trail junction and asked the last walker to stay within sight.'),
    (57, 3, 'A bright chart showed the experiment''s average result as well as its unusual trial.'),
    (58, 3, 'The post office changed its notice after residents described where they had become lost.'),
    (59, 3, 'The organizer left room for slower walkers and checked that the ramp was clear.'),
    (60, 3, 'Their final report explained the method, the limits, and what the group would test next.'),
    (61, 4, 'An inventory is useful only when its dates and locations can be checked against the items themselves.'),
    (62, 4, 'The canal team postponed its repair until daylight; fragile stones near the bank required care.'),
    (63, 4, 'A street can change its purpose long before an official map changes the name printed beside it.'),
    (64, 4, 'The thermometer near the roof gave a higher reading than the one beside the shaded table.'),
    (65, 4, 'Instead of declaring the bowl a cooking vessel, the exhibit described what had actually been found.'),
    (66, 4, 'During the drill, a delivery cart blocked half the corridor; the leader recorded the hazard.'),
    (67, 4, 'Both sides of the letter were scanned in order, preserving the change in ink after midnight.'),
    (68, 4, 'The cheapest estimate omitted an important fitting, so the students compared complete costs.'),
    (69, 4, 'Footmarks curved around the orchard''s low ground, which flooded after heavy rain.'),
    (70, 4, 'One hand signal resembled a casual wave; the team replaced it before the machines started.'),
    (71, 4, 'A catalog entry should distinguish a draft map from the polished drawing prepared months later.'),
